hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"395","It is narrated by Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj, it is narrated by Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghayath, it is narrated by Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwaith, he said: A man and I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he bid us farewell, then said: “When you travel and the time for prayer comes, then give the call to prayer and perform the iqama, and let them lead you in prayer.” “The eldest of you.” The shoe said: They were close in recitation."
"396","It was narrated on the authority of Salam bin Junada, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, who said: We came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I and a cousin of mine, and he said: “When you travel, then give the call to prayer and perform the iqaamah, and let the eldest of you lead in prayer.”"
